# A panel whose scanline is padded past the visible width, which is what
# the ASUS TUF reported (1920x1080, stride 2048) and what no other bed
# here can present. Small on purpose: 512x240 is 123k pixels, the same
# order as gop-scene-viewport's scratch panel, and the 192 pad columns
# make a width-stepping renderer fail loudly rather than by one pixel.
-gop -gop-width 320 -gop-height 240 -gop-stride 512
